# Used only when building the Android app shell (npm run build:capacitor / cap:sync).
# The native app's bundled HTML/JS is loaded from capacitor://localhost, not from the real
# server, so — unlike the plain website build — it must be told the backend's real address
# explicitly; same-origin detection in api/client.ts has nothing to detect it from here.
#
# Update this the day the VPS gets a real domain + HTTPS (see DEPLOY.md) — plain http:// only
# works because android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml explicitly allows cleartext traffic
# for this internal tool; that's a real trade-off (unencrypted login/API traffic), not a default
# to keep long-term.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://77.37.45.106
